From ef7a805b082132f3e1dc93ccdfb15a0a69fe981c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Forst <ensonador@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:41:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] ble/shim: provide usr_timeout_del in the Bluetooth-only
 build

AC79NN_SDK_V1.2.14's btctrler.a calls usr_timeout_del from multilink_schedule.c.o
even when the config cuts multilinking down to LE_ADV | LE_SLAVE. The symbol
lived only in ble/wifi/wifi_shim.c, so LOOM-8 v0.8.1's Bluetooth build (SDK
V1.2.14) failed to link with "undefined reference to usr_timeout_del". Define it
in the Bluetooth timer shim beside usr_timer_del, guarded by !SHIM_WIFI because
the Wi-Fi shim owns the name there. It deletes a timer like JieLi's hardware
timer path does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ble/shim/systimer.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ble/shim/systimer.c b/ble/shim/systimer.c
index b58eabd..9a19582 100644
--- a/ble/shim/systimer.c
+++ b/ble/shim/systimer.c
@@ -84,6 +84,12 @@ u16 usr_timeout_add(void *priv, void (*fn)(void *), u32 msec, u8 prio)
 void sys_timer_del(u16 id) { stimer_t *t = get(id); if (t) t->used = 0; }
 void sys_timeout_del(u16 id) { sys_timer_del(id); }
 void usr_timer_del(u16 id) { sys_timer_del(id); }
+/* AC79NN_SDK_V1.2.14's btctrler.a (multilink_schedule.c.o) calls this even in the trimmed peripheral
+ * build; the Wi-Fi shim had it, the Bluetooth one did not, so the link failed (Wi-Fi's owns the name
+ * there) */
+#if !SHIM_WIFI
+void usr_timeout_del(u16 id) { sys_timer_del(id); }
+#endif
 int sys_timer_modify(u16 id, u32 msec)
 {
     stimer_t *t = get(id);
